# META-PREFIX-DECODE over a running turn. The fake gateway holds the answer
# after six chunks (`held`), so the turn is running for every key below.
# (a) `ESC ESC [ A`: fx's meta-prefixed Up, a paragraph move
# (escape_parser.zig:552-555, :561-568, :83-89@481104fd), and no Escape: the
# turn runs on and nothing is armed. (b) Two Escape bytes in one burst: one
# Escape (terminal_action_decoder.zig:84-88, :174-183), which arms the
# interrupt (app_input_runtime.zig:2740-2758); past its 1 s window
# (gesture_state.zig:5) the turn is still running. (c) A person's two
# presses, 0.3 s apart: the second stops the turn.
gateway p5-cancel-double-escape-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
type stream please
wait 1
key Enter
held
wait 1
snap mid
key -H 1b 1b 5b 41
wait 0.6
snap a-meta-up
key Escape Escape
wait 1.5
snap b-burst-running
key Escape
wait 0.3
key Escape
wait 2
snap c-person-cancelled
release
wait 1
gwlog
